<anchor xml:id="_structai_skeleton_bone_1a699e4965860b358dc210deb1bf143305"/><section>
    <title>mOffsetMatrix</title>
<indexterm><primary>mOffsetMatrix</primary><secondary>aiSkeletonBone</secondary></indexterm>
<indexterm><primary>aiSkeletonBone</primary><secondary>mOffsetMatrix</secondary></indexterm>
<para><computeroutput><link linkend="_defs_8h_1ab51df4230ceb602bbc1bc109c432a6a0">C_STRUCT</link> <link linkend="_structai_matrix4x4">aiMatrix4x4</link> aiSkeletonBone::mOffsetMatrix</computeroutput></para>
<para>Matrix that transforms from bone space to mesh space in bind pose.</para>

<para>This matrix describes the position of the mesh in the local space of this bone when the skeleton was bound. Thus it can be used directly to determine a desired vertex position, given the world-space transform of the bone when animated, and the position of the vertex in mesh space.</para>

<para>It is sometimes called an inverse-bind matrix, or inverse bind pose matrix. </para>
</section>
